#ROOM
Vnum     50800
Name     Pelagian Orbital Institute~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     You have arrived at Pelagian Orbital Institute, a training station in orbit
above LHS 1140 b. This academy teaches the basic commands needed to survive,
travel and interact with other people in the wider interstellar community.
Each compartment has a specific lesson. Explore the academy in full and read
each room carefully. The student message area is to the west; return here
afterward and continue north when you are ready.

The entrance concourse reflects its builders: smooth pressure-rated walls,
blue-green glass and channels of circulating water. Through the nearest
observation panel you can see LHS 1140 b filling the observation windows
beneath the station.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50801
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50930
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50801
Name     Pelagian Instruction Spine~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor links the academy's first instructional rooms. The language and
communication lesson is to the west, while practical skill instruction is to
the east. When you have finished with both rooms, return here and continue
north.

The passage is built around smooth pressure-rated walls, blue-green glass and
channels of circulating water, with cool aquatic light that ripples softly
across polished surfaces. Displays along the wall present Pelagian navigation
charts, oceanographic models and engineering memorials.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50803
Desc      The Laboratory of Skills.
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50800
Desc      Entrance to Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50806
Desc      Abbigayle's Language Lessons.
~
#ENDEXIT

#MUDPROG
Progtype  leave_prog~
Arglist   100~
Comlist   if isimmort($n)
else
  mpforce $n vis
endif
~
#ENDPROG

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50802
Name     Pelagian Navigation Success Annex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     You completed the navigation exercise successfully. Continue north to return
to the reference room and resume the academy course.

A small window in this quiet annex looks toward LHS 1140 b, a reminder that
the entire training complex is an orbital station.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50803
Name     Pelagian Skills Laboratory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This is the academy's practical skills laboratory. Type PRACTICE to see the
abilities currently available to you. Your list may include weapon skills,
general skills, languages and other advanced abilities. To improve something,
use PRACTICE <full skill name>.

For example, to practice dual wield, type PRAC DUAL WIELD. Additional
proficiency is gained through training and successful use. Type HELP PRACTICE
or HELP <skill> whenever you need more information.

Pelagian instructors favor a Pelagian doctrine emphasizing control,
coordination and technical preparation. The room itself is equipped with
precise engineering consoles with redundant environmental and pressure
monitoring.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50801
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50840 1 50803
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50804
Name     Pelagian Reference Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors silence~
Desc     This quiet reference room suppresses most public channels so that students can
read without interruption. Type CHAN for a list of channels. You can disable a
channel with CHAN -<channel>, enable it with CHAN +<channel>, or use CHAN -ALL
and CHAN +ALL to silence or restore them together.

When you are ready, go west for the navigation exercise. Follow the room
descriptions until you find your way back here. If you become lost, the up
route returns you to this room. Once you have completed the exercise, continue
north.

The archive contains Pelagian navigation charts, oceanographic models and
engineering memorials. cool aquatic light that ripples softly across polished
surfaces keeps the room comfortable for long periods of study.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50814
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50801
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50807
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50805
Name     Pelagian Combat Trials Control~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     This chamber is reserved for controlled combat trials. In ordinary play you
will encounter mobiles, often shortened to MOBS. Some may be aggressive and
attack as soon as you enter their location. Defeating opponents can provide
experience and loot.

After a fight, EXAMINE CORPSE and GET ALL CORPSE can be used to inspect and
recover items. CONFIG +AUTOLOOT and related configuration options can automate
parts of this process. REST, SLEEP, WAKE and STAND are useful while recovering
between exercises.

The chamber is arranged around a Pelagian doctrine emphasizing control,
coordination and technical preparation, with smooth pressure-rated walls,
blue-green glass and channels of circulating water protecting the rest of the
station from the training area.
~
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50806
Name     Pelagian Language and Culture Suite~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This room teaches the language system. Type PRACTICE to see languages
available to you. Your native tongue and the common language are normally
available without additional study. To learn another language, use LANGUAGE
LEARN <language>.

For more information use HELP LANGUAGES, HELP SPEAK and HELP TONGUE. Language
study consumes practice sessions, and capable students generally learn more
efficiently.

The walls carry Pelagian navigation charts, oceanographic models and
engineering memorials, giving students examples of how language, history and
identity developed among the Pelagian.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50801
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50894 1 50806
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50807
Name     Pelagian Orientation Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is the beginning of the navigation exercise. Type CONFIG +AUTOEXIT if you
want obvious exits displayed automatically. EXIT lists visible routes, and
LOOK <direction> lets you inspect an adjoining direction before moving.

Your next route is west. Try EXIT and LOOK WEST before moving on. The exercise
uses smooth pressure-rated walls, blue-green glass and channels of circulating
water to make each section visually distinct without changing the station's
underlying layout.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50809
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy, it looks safe
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    Door~
ExDesc       You see a solid oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50808
Name     Pelagian Combat Practice Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is a controlled combat practice bay. A restrained training creature is
used here to demonstrate attacking, judging an opponent and withdrawing from a
fight. The CONSIDER command compares your character with a potential opponent;
elsewhere, use CON <MOBNAME> before attacking something unfamiliar.

The bay follows a Pelagian doctrine emphasizing control, coordination and
technical preparation. Heavy barriers and precise engineering consoles with
redundant environmental and pressure monitoring keep the exercise isolated
from the inhabited sections of the station.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50816
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50845 1 50808
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50809
Name     Pelagian Sealed-Access Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This section teaches doors and less-obvious exits. A closed door may not be
listed among obvious exits until you interact with it. Read the room
description, LOOK <direction>, try moving into a direction, and use OPEN
<direction> or OPEN DOOR when appropriate. HELP OPEN provides more detail.

cool aquatic light that ripples softly across polished surfaces and
deliberately repetitive wall panels make the exercise depend on observation
rather than decoration.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50810
Desc      An Enclosed Room
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50807
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50811
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 50809 0 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see a solid oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50810
Name     Pelagian Discovery Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     You found the enclosed chamber. Hidden or closed rooms like this appear
throughout the game, sometimes with obvious clues and sometimes with very
subtle ones. LOOK, EXIT and careful reading are your most reliable tools.

The compact chamber uses smooth pressure-rated walls, blue-green glass and
channels of circulating water. Its plain construction is intentional: the
lesson is to notice access routes rather than rely on elaborate scenery.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50809
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 50810 2 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50811
Name     Pelagian Hidden-Route Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This passage introduces special and hidden exits. Hidden routes may not be
found simply by walking into every wall. Read descriptions, inspect mobiles
and objects, and look for words that might identify a door or route.

Locked exits may require a key or an appropriate skill. Directions can be
abbreviated as N, E, W, S, NE, NW, SE, SW, U and D. Some special routes use a
word such as LEAVE, CLIMB or ENTER. Continue north and use the next room's
description to find the concealed route.

The Pelagian design language here uses smooth pressure-rated walls, blue-green
glass and channels of circulating water, making small visual details
especially important.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50812
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50809
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50812
Name     Pelagian Heritage Salon~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This chamber has been furnished as a Pelagian heritage salon. A broad table
and twelve seats dominate the center while exhibits of Pelagian navigation
charts, oceanographic models and engineering memorials line the walls. One
wall display appears slightly different from the others.

Use LOOK <word> on details mentioned in the room. Sometimes inspecting one
object reveals the clue needed to discover a hidden exit. The exercise is
unchanged mechanically; only the station's cultural presentation differs.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50811
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50813
Desc      door
~
Keywords  tapestry door~
Flags     isdoor closed secret~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 50812 3 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    tapestry~
ExDesc       Upon closer inspection you realise that this is not even a tapestry, but
a cunningly camouflaged wall! You can see the outline of a door as you
look closer.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    west~
ExDesc       You see a tapestry on the wall here, something just isn't right about it.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    w~
ExDesc       You see a tapestry on the wall.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see a cleverly disguised door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    Crystal globes~
ExDesc       This globes cast shadows in the corners. The shadows on the west
tapestry almost appears to be an opening.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50813
Name     Pelagian Maintenance Alcove~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     You found the concealed alcove. Secret rooms can contain useful items, clues
or alternate routes, so careful reading often pays off. This room also
demonstrates a special SOMEWHERE exit. Inspect the picture and nearby wall if
you want to discover the intended route, or use the obvious up exit to return.

The alcove exposes precise engineering consoles with redundant environmental
and pressure monitoring, giving the space the feel of a hidden service
compartment inside Pelagian Orbital Institute.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50812
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction somewhere~
ToRoom    50802
Keywords  crack~
Flags     hidden auto~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 50813 1 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see an oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    picture~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    crack~
ExDesc       This is a huge CRACK, you could probably squeeze through it. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    wall~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50814
Name     Pelagian Readiness Concourse~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor introduces commands used to inspect your character. SCORE shows
core statistics, EQUIPMENT lists worn items, INVENTORY shows carried items,
and LEVEL reports advancement information. Common abbreviations include SC, EQ
and I.

Use HELP <subject> for additional information. The concourse is finished with
smooth pressure-rated walls, blue-green glass and channels of circulating
water, and cool aquatic light that ripples softly across polished surfaces
clearly marks the route toward combat training.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50815
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50804
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50815
Name     Pelagian Combat Briefing Deck~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Combat training is immediately ahead. You can begin an ordinary fight with
KILL <mob>, while many learned skills and abilities can also initiate combat.
Before attacking unfamiliar opponents, use CONSIDER and review the help for
your available abilities.

Remember that aggressive actions against another player can have consequences.
The briefing deck reflects a Pelagian doctrine emphasizing control,
coordination and technical preparation; precise engineering consoles with
redundant environmental and pressure monitoring monitors the practice bay
below.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50817
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50814
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    50816
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50816
Name     Pelagian Withdrawal Training Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     This bay explains ways to leave a dangerous fight. WIMPY can automatically
withdraw you when your hit points fall below a chosen threshold. FLEE attempts
an immediate manual withdrawal. Emergency recall or extraction mechanics may
also exist, but they generally carry a greater cost and should be treated as a
last resort.

The room is intentionally austere, with smooth pressure-rated walls,
blue-green glass and channels of circulating water and clear route markers
designed to make emergency instructions easy to understand.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50808
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50815
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50817
Name     Pelagian Recovery Lounge~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Long fights and long journeys require recovery. REST is the safest ordinary
way to recover. SLEEP can recover more deeply but leaves you vulnerable in
unsafe locations. Use WAKE after sleeping and STAND after resting.

Characters can also become hungry or thirsty. Ask the service unit here for
food or a canteen, then use EAT <item> or DRINK <item>. The fountain can also
be used directly or to refill a container.

This is a humidified commons with flowing water features and quiet acoustic
baffling. Beyond the windows lies LHS 1140 b filling the observation windows
beneath the station.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50827
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50815
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 50815 1 50817
Reset M 0 50865 1 50817
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50818
Name     Pelagian Object Interaction Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Some items that initially appear unimportant can become useful later. Speak
with the student here and pay attention to what they have found.

Containers can hold other objects. Use LOOK IN <container>, GET <item> FROM
<container>, PUT <item> IN <container>, and OPEN <container> when necessary.

Hint: say hello. The exercise occupies a small Pelagian student annex fitted
with precise engineering consoles with redundant environmental and pressure
monitoring.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50822
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50842 1 50818
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50819
Name     Pelagian Fabrication Loft~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Some objects are obtained by manipulating, combining or crafting other
objects. Your character may eventually learn specialized crafting skills;
other situations are as simple as opening a container or operating a control.

This compact fabrication loft is dense with precise engineering consoles with
redundant environmental and pressure monitoring. It mirrors the practical
working style found throughout Pelagian Orbital Institute.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    50822
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 50818 1 50819
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50820
Name     Pelagian Salvage Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A common way to acquire equipment is to recover it from defeated mobiles.
After defeating the training unit here, use EXAMINE CORPSE to inspect what it
carried and GET ALL FROM CORPSE to recover the contents. Configuration options
can automate looting or currency collection.

The salvage exercise takes place in a reinforced work cell equipped with
precise engineering consoles with redundant environmental and pressure
monitoring and arranged according to a Pelagian doctrine emphasizing control,
coordination and technical preparation.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50822
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50860 1 50820
  Reset E 1 50801 1 8
  Reset E 1 50802 1 13
  Reset G 1 50804 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50821
Name     Pelagian Academy Supply Exchange~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Shops are useful for acquiring equipment and selling items you no longer need.
LIST shows a merchant's stock, BUY <object> purchases something, SELL <object>
offers an item for sale, and VALUE <object> asks what the merchant will pay.

The backpack is particularly useful because it can hold spare equipment. This
supply exchange is decorated with Pelagian navigation charts, oceanographic
models and engineering memorials and uses precise engineering consoles with
redundant environmental and pressure monitoring for inventory and transaction
handling.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50822
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50870 1 50821
  Reset G 1 50817 1
  Reset G 1 50811 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50822
Name     Pelagian Equipment Acquisition Lab~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Finding better equipment is an important part of progression. Some methods
become available only after learning the appropriate skills, including SEARCH
and DIG. Other methods may carry legal or social consequences.

The rooms east, west, above and below demonstrate different ways to obtain
useful items. Explore all four, then continue north.

This equipment lab uses smooth pressure-rated walls, blue-green glass and
channels of circulating water; lockers and work surfaces are sized and
arranged for Pelagian trainees.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50823
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50820
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50827
Flags     isdoor~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    50821
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50819
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    50818
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50823
Name     Pelagian Final Navigation Challenge~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     You are almost finished. The graduation hall is immediately north, but the
door is locked. The child here appears upset and may know how to open it.
Finding and returning the child's lost toy should help.

Hints: find the lost toy give the toy to the child ask about the key

The final challenge takes place beneath displays of Pelagian navigation
charts, oceanographic models and engineering memorials.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50824
Key       50923
Flags     isdoor closed locked~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50822
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50843 1 50823
Reset D 0 50823 0 2
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50824
Name     Pelagian Graduation Gallery~
Sector   city~
Desc     You completed the academy course. Proceed through the graduation gallery,
receive your diploma and continue toward the docking bay.

The gallery is a transparent orbital walkway attached to Pelagian Orbital
Institute. Instead of a city beneath you, the windows reveal LHS 1140 b
filling the observation windows beneath the station. Structural ribs frame the
corridor while traffic lights from local shuttles move silently beyond the
glass.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50823
Flags     isdoor~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    50825
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50850 1 50824
Reset O 0 50914 1 50824
Reset D 0 50824 2 0
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50825
Name     LHS 1140 b Orbital Dock~
Sector   city~
Desc     This docking bay projects from the academy station so that training shuttles
can approach without crossing the inhabited modules. Guidance lights, docking
clamps and service equipment line the perimeter.

Beyond the bay you can see LHS 1140 b filling the observation windows beneath
the station. A small shuttle is waiting to carry graduates down toward LHS
1140 b. To board it, use ENTER.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    50824
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction somewhere~
ToRoom    50826
Flags     hidden can_enter~
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 50822 1 50825
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50826
Name     LHS 1140 b Planetfall Shuttle~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob~
Desc     You are inside a compact planetfall shuttle. Passenger seats sit directly
behind the pilot position, with a small service compartment at the rear. The
craft carries newly graduated students from Pelagian Orbital Institute toward
LHS 1140 b.

Give your diploma to the pilot when requested. If you do not yet have one, use
LEAVE and return to the graduation area.
~
#EXIT
Direction somewhere~
ToRoom    50825
Flags     hidden can_leave~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50855 1 50826
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50827
Name     Pelagian Continuity Briefing~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob indoors prototype~
Desc     The final briefing concerns character continuity and recovery after death. In
this setting death can carry severe consequences, so make use of whatever
medical, backup or continuity services the wider game provides. Update those
safeguards regularly rather than waiting until after a major loss.

The briefing chamber uses precise engineering consoles with redundant
environmental and pressure monitoring, while a status display shows the
orbital position of Pelagian Orbital Institute above LHS 1140 b.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    50822
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    50817
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 50895 1 50827
Reset D 0 50827 0 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50899
Name     Pelagian Academy Program Service Room~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob~Desc     This sealed service room exists for academy mobile programs and should not be
removed. Maintenance labels identify it as part of Pelagian Orbital
Institute's internal automation network.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50900
Name     Pelagian Academy Test Workshop~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob factory~Desc     A small test workshop used by academy staff. Benches, diagnostic ports and
precise engineering consoles with redundant environmental and pressure
monitoring fill the room.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50901
Name     Pelagian Quiet Test Compartment~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob safe silence~Desc     A deliberately quiet compartment isolated from the busier academy modules.
cool aquatic light that ripples softly across polished surfaces and
sound-damped surfaces make it suitable for testing or study.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50929
Name     Pelagian Isolated Test Chamber~
Sector   city~
Flags    nomob prototype~Desc     This isolated test chamber is intentionally featureless. Instrument panels
from precise engineering consoles with redundant environmental and pressure
monitoring are the only obvious connection to the rest of Pelagian Orbital
Institute.
~

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     50930
Name     Pelagian Student Commons~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob safe~
Desc     This is the academy student commons, a final safe place to rest, read and
practice using the message system. Use NOTE LIST to list messages, NOTE READ
<msgnum> to read one, and HELP NOTE for additional commands.

The room is a humidified commons with flowing water features and quiet
acoustic baffling. The station windows give occasional views of LHS 1140 b
filling the observation windows beneath the station.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    50800
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 50914 1 50930
#ENDROOM

